{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqkSFc6HECYkKNjZ8C54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled TC-254's latest amendment a change of meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=1`), blessed it, and re-anchored it. Both commits carry the `WI: WI-866` trailer, and the pre-commit hooks passed.\n\n**Why meaning:** one Method clause changed when the hand claim must land to trigger the refusal. It used to be \"between the close and the merge\"; now it is \"after the close and before the successor mint\". The window now also covers the stretch after the merge and before the mint. An implementation that refused only for claims before the merge would pass the old text and fail the new one.\n\n**Why I blessed it:** the new window is the one the cited test actually uses. `test_a_row_claimed_between_close_and_merge_refuses_the_whole_mint` merges first, then claims WI-402, then runs `intake_after_merge`. The old wording named a window the test never exercises, so the amendment makes the clause accurate. Every other clause is byte-identical to the text I blessed last sitting.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `a3169b34` — the verdict file only.\n- `b15f971a` — the re-attestation. I ran `snapshot --reattests TC-254`, which recorded act 66 with `reattested = [\"TC-254\"]` and copied only `test-cases.toml`. No registry cell changed, and I checked that the copy matches the live registry.\n\n**For the coordinator:** this lane now holds acts 64 to 66, and WI-860's lane also used `seq = 64` for its approval. When the second of the two lanes merges, `acts.toml` will need its sequence numbers reconciled.\n\nI left the `.requested` marker alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":624,"cache_read_input_tokens":244527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":624},"output_tokens":543,"service_tier":"standard","